<section id="how-it-works">
  <h2>How Distilled works, in one paragraph</h2>
  <p>You install a read-only GitHub App on the repositories you want to track. GitHub then sends Distilled a webhook every time a pull request opens, closes or merges, and every time a deployment succeeds or a release is published. Distilled turns those events into six metrics, links each merged pull request to the deployment that shipped it, and recomputes the trends hourly. There is nothing to instrument, no agent to run, and no manual data entry. Every number traces back to a real pull request or deployment, so you can always ask why it says what it says.</p>
  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>Distilled does not backfill.</strong> Tracking starts from your next GitHub event, not from your repository's history. Expect the dashboard to fill out over the first few weeks. <a href="/docs/data-quality">Data quality</a> covers how to tell when the numbers are ready to act on.</p>
  </div>
</section>

